# The Actions deployment workflow, held out of the repository on purpose.
#
# It publishes through `actions/deploy-pages`, which only works once the repository's Pages
# source is switched from a branch to GitHub Actions. That source is currently the `gh-pages`
# branch (`build_type: legacy`), so committing the workflow would put a failing run on every
# push while the site carried on being served from the branch. The file stays on disk as the
# ready-made second half of that change; flipping the source is the first half, and it is a
# repository setting rather than a commit.
.github/workflows/deploy.yml
